{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1173713-monsters-for-my-chronicle","id":1173713,"title":"Monsters for my Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-06T00:19:51-08:00","id":1173713,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Monsters for my Chronicle","content":"My very first M20 chronicle is in the present (2018), with fantasy beasts and monsters lurking in the shadows (like Supernatural TV show).<br /> I am looking for appropriate stat blocks for the following creatures:<br /> --&gt; Imp<br /> --&gt; Goblin<br /> --&gt; Nymph<br /> --&gt; Hellhound<br /> --&gt; Lesser Vampire<br /> --&gt; Greater Vampire<br /> <br /> Any assistance is greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> Thanks - Drunken Uraak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23654-drunkenuraak","name":"DrunkenUraak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T02:39:08-08:00","id":1173719,"title":"","content":"Depending on how thorough you want to be, you can crack open either Vampire or Changeling to stat these creatures up, or just make the stats up based on DnD.<br /> <br /> Mage revised core has some good quick and dirty vampire stats in the back which can be good. Everything else can be spirit\u2019s taken from Axis Mundi. A water nymph, for example, could easily be a repurposed water elemental.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to do it though is to just decide how strong they should be and roll the appropriate number of dice during the session. I personally feel stating up each individual monster for every combat to be rather a waste of time, but having a generic stat sheet for \u201cweak enemy, medium.enemy, strong enemy, smart enemy\u201d etc, can be just as effective, with a small list of species specific powers on the side.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s all about cutting down on the paperwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-06-2018, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T04:11:02-08:00","id":1173726,"title":"","content":"The bygone <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/The_Bygone_Bestiary\" target=\"_blank\">Bestiary</a> might be of help...as It's meant for that type of inclusion. <br /> <br /> You probably could get the PDF (and possibly Print on Demand) at DriveThruRPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Nigh